I go to the billing counter.
There are many things in my shopping cart.
There is rice, lentils, tea powder, and spices in the cart.
I see a cashier there.
He takes my items one by one.
He scans everything.
"The total is eight hundred and fifty rupees," he says.
I give him the money.
He gives me the bill.
"Do you want a plastic bag?" he asks.
"I do not want a plastic bag," I say.
"I have a cloth bag."
I like cloth bags very much.
I put the heavy rice and lentils in the bag first.
Then I put the tea powder and spices.
The bag is very heavy.
I go out of the supermarket with the items.
